# Hybrid variant: ONE stick for AMD and modern NVIDIA machines.
#
#   - AMD: Mesa/RADV graphics (common packages) + the system ROCm PyTorch.
#   - NVIDIA (Turing -> RTX 50): the open kernel modules; CUDA PyTorch is baked
#     to /opt/bench-pypackages and selected at run time by the live launcher
#     (see bench/Run-LinuxBench.sh) - no static .pth, so AMD keeps ROCm.
#
# Legacy NVIDIA (Maxwell/Pascal/Volta) needs the 580 branch and stays its own
# variant; it cannot coexist with nvidia-open (both own the nvidia module).
python-pytorch-rocm
rocm-smi-lib
rocminfo
hsa-rocr
nvidia-open
nvidia-utils
nvidia-settings
